<title>USA: USDA to donate U.S. farm goods to Kyrgyzstan.</title>
<headline>USDA to donate U.S. farm goods to Kyrgyzstan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Friday said it will donate about 1,500 tonnes of U.S. commodities to the American Red Cross to distribute to the needy in Kyrgyzstan.</p>
<p>USDA said the donated goods include 600 tonnes of wheat flour, 600 tonnes of rice and 300 tonnes of vegetable oil.</p>
<p>The donation will be made under USDA's Food for Progress program and the supply period is fiscal year 1996.</p>
</text>
